@startuml
title libmxl-monitoring - Components
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "Process reading or writing MXL flows" {
  [Media loop\nreads / writes MXL flows] as Loop
  package "mxl-monitoring (static)" {
    [Wrappers\nreader.h / writer.h] as Wrap
    [Content checks\ncontent.h] as Content
    [Core model\nmonitoring.h\nflows, counters,\nsnapshots, events] as Core
  }
  package "Exporters (static, optional)" {
    [mxl-monitoring-prometheus\ntext exposition] as Prom
    [mxl-monitoring-http\nGET /metrics, /healthz] as Http
    [mxl-monitoring-otlp\nOTLP/HTTP push] as Otlp
  }
}
[libmxl.so] as Mxl
cloud "Prometheus\n(scrapes)" as PromBackend
cloud "OTel Collector" as Collector

Loop --> Wrap : libmxl calls
Wrap --> Mxl : forwards unchanged
Wrap --> Content : check grains / samples
Wrap --> Core : record outcome\n(atomics, never blocks)
Loop --> Core : mxlMonitoringPoll\n(one thread)
Prom --> Core : snapshot
Http --> Prom : render
Otlp --> Core : snapshot + events
Http --> PromBackend : text format
Otlp --> Collector : OTLP/HTTP

note bottom of Core
  One context per process,
  one flow handle per flow.
  Recording touches only its
  own flow's atomics.
end note
@enduml
